<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Saindhava dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">735 CE – 920 CE (approx.) · capital Bhutambilika</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of western Saurashtra that ruled from Bhutambilika and fought Arab raiders from the sea.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Saindhavas established themselves in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, around the early 8th century, probably after the decline of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/maitraka-dynasty">Maitraka dynasty</a>. Their founder was Pushyadeva, and their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghumli">Bhutambilika</a>, modern Ghumli near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/porbandar-state">Porbandar</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty is known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants dated in the Gupta era. They record that King Agguka I defeated a naval attack, probably by Arab raiders, which shows the dynasty's role in guarding the coast. The Saindhavas were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivas</a> and appear to have acknowledged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara</a> as overlords at times.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Saindhava line disappears after the early 10th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghumli">Ghumli</a> later became a seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jethwa-dynasty">Jethwa</a> rulers of the region.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/saindhava-dynasty.jpg" alt="Saindhava dynasty" width="320" height="166"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Michel Moullec from Vern sur Seiche (35, Bretagne), France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I56_Saindhavas_drachme_1_(8097356527).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>735 CE – 920 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bhutambilika</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pushyadeva, Agguka I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shaivism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Saindhavas of Saurashtra</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=828&amp;focus=saindhava-dynasty" aria-label="Saindhava dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6551 1369 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Saindhava dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6871 1625L7103 1442"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6871 1625h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6871 1625h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=828&amp;focus=saindhava-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

